      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Muzaffarnagar Insured</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Transporting a two-wheeler to or from Muzaffarnagar requires meticulous preparation to ensure a smooth, secure, and legally compliant journey. Whether you are relocating, shifting for work, or sending a vehicle to a relative, having the correct documentation is paramount.</p>
<p>Inadequate paperwork can lead to delays at transit hubs, potential legal issues, or disputes during delivery. This guide outlines the essential documents you must gather before handing over your bike to a transport provider.</p>

<p>First and foremost, you must provide a self-attested photocopy of the Registered Certificate (RC). The self-attestation, which involves signing the copy and writing your name, date, and place, verifies the authenticity of the document without requiring the original to be kept in transit. This helps the transporter verify the vehicle's identity and legal ownership status.</p>
<p>Additionally, a valid Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate is mandatory. This ensures that your vehicle meets the current environmental standards set by the Regional Transport Office (RTO). An expired PUC can result in fines or refusal of transport, so ensure this document is current before scheduling your shipment.</p>

<p>Equally critical is a valid insurance certificate. Verify that the policy is active and covers the period of transit. While standard insurance covers third-party liability, it may not fully cover comprehensive damage during transport.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Therefore, it is highly recommended to purchase 100% declared-value marine transit insurance.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This specialized coverage protects the full market value of your bike against accidental damage, theft, or loss while in the custody of the logistics company.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Insist on a policy that explicitly states "100% declared value" to ensure you are not underinsured in the event of a claim.</span></li></ul>

<p>Finally, the IBA-approved consignment bilty is the single most important logistical document. The Indian Banks Association (IBA) sets standards for safe transport documentation. The bilty serves as a receipt and a contract of carriage, detailing the shipper, consignee, vehicle details, and estimated delivery time.</p>
<p>Without a proper IBA-approved bilty, you have no legal recourse if the vehicle is lost or damaged. Keep the original bilty safe; the receiving party will need to present it along with their ID proof to collect the vehicle.</p>

